    "abstract": "<jats:p>At present, the global energy supply is generally sufficient but the str ucture is tight. Supercapacitors have the characteristics of high power density, extremely fast charging and \ndischarging, long cycle life, and wide operating temperature range. This article reviews the research progress of the application of biomass-based materials in supercapacitor electrode materials, and elaborately discusses the types of biomass materials, their preparation methods, the structure and working principle of supercapacitors, as well as the performance of biomass-based materials as electrode materials. Biological-based materials can significantly enhance the performance of supercapacitors through various preparation methods. In particular, biomass carbon materials, due to their high specific surface area and excellent conductivity, have become a research hotspot for electrode materials in supercapacitors. This article provides a theoretical basis for future research to further optimize the preparation process of biomass-based materials and enhance their electrochemical performance, thereby promoting their development in practical applications.</jats:p>",
